# The Vercel deploy serves the repo root so that `vercel.json` can live here and
# no dashboard Root Directory setting is needed. Everything except the web
# surface is therefore excluded — without this, the vision doc, the domain
# glossary and the entire app and prototype source would be publicly fetchable
# at their repo paths.
#
# This is a denylist rather than a deny-all-then-re-allow. `*` followed by
# `!web/**` looks tidier and does not work: the exclusion is applied before the
# `rewrites` in vercel.json resolve, so `/` and `/privacy` rewrite onto files
# that were never uploaded and both 404. Verified against `vercel dev`.
#
# `app/src/__tests__/web-surface.test.ts` pins this list against the repo's
# top-level entries, so adding a directory fails the suite rather than silently
# publishing it.

app
prototype
docs
supabase
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
pushup-counter-vision.md
